What is Exit Code?

Every Linux command returns a status.

0 = Success

1-255 = Failure

Check Exit Code:

ls

echo $?

Production Example
systemctl restart nginx

if [ $? -eq 0 ]
then
    echo "Restart Success"
else
    echo "Restart Failed"
fi

Strict Error Handling
set -e

Stops script when an error occurs.

Debug Mode
set -x

Shows each command during execution.
